  "answer": "Targeted FY26 productivity ($500m) is insufficient to restore positive jaws; it primarily offsets continuing investment pressure. In FY25, operating expenses rose 9% (to $11,916m), with ex-restructuring growth at 6% [ev-1]. Staff costs increased 7% ($6,326m) due to wage growth and banker investments, while technology costs surged 13% ($3,136m) driven by UNITE [ev-2], [ev-3]. The expense-to-income ratio widened from 50.3% to 53.0% [ev-8]. Investment spend reached $1,918m, with UNITE accounting for 34% ($660m) and a high 74% expensing rate [ev-11], [ev-12]. This heavy expensing profile means the $500m FY26 savings target will be largely consumed by ongoing UNITE and wage inflation, preventing meaningful jaw expansion.",
